{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1240,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the most amazing things about atoms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3680,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that they're mainly empty space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6320,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If an atom were as wide as your arm span,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9160,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then the electrons would all be whizzing about\ninside the volume enclosed by your fingertips,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14280,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "meanwhile the nucleus would be sitting in the center,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17180,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and its diameter would be smaller\nthan the width of a single human hair..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23140,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So all of the atoms that make up you and me"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25900,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and all the seemingly solid things in the universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29260,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are mostly empty space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31320,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this is incredible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32820,
    "dDurationMs": 6600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what is even more mind-boggling\nis that empty space is not truly empty..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39420,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I know because I've seen it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41480,
    "dDurationMs": 2780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a simulation by Prof. Derek Leinweber\nat the University of Adelaide."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46420,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was made using a supercomputer to crunch the calculations of Quantum Chromo-Dynamics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51860,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that is the theory of\nfundamental particles called 'quarks',"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55860,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the building blocks of protons and neutrons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58620,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and how they interact with each other through 'gluons'."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61980,
    "dDurationMs": 5780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What you're looking at here is the energy density\nof the gluon field fluctuations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67760,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Where('s) the little red spots come out,\nthe energy density is very high..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71720,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it fades down through the colors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73520,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, in the lowest energy, the field fluctuations\nare not rendering in this animation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78120,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so we can actually see into it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79940,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what we see is a bubbling soup\nof quantum field fluctuations,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84140,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that come and go incredibly quickly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86740,
    "dDurationMs": 6180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The frame rate of this simulation is one million billion billion frames per second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92920,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that is truly high speed..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95580,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The dimensions of this box are absolutely tiny."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99200,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are millionth of a billionth of a meter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102660,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "roughly enough space to stick two protons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105780,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there are no protons here..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107580,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a simulation of the vacuum on its own,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110880,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what we normally think of as 'empty space'."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113860,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Empty space is actually full of this\nquark-and-gluon field fluctuations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119160,
    "dDurationMs": 8600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, on average, it is possible to annihilate a quark\nfrom empty space, 'cause it's not empty...!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127880,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That just sounds like the most ridiculous idea that ..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130460,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're meant to have empty space,\n and yet you can go and get rid of stuff from it..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135580,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's right. So it isn't empty !"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137480,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now it seems counterintuitive that the vacuum\nat its lowest energy state should contain all of this stuff."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143440,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, in fact, to clear out the fluctuations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146340,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and create a truly empty vacuum\nwould require a lot of energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151060,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The empty vacuum actually costs\nan enormous amount of energy to create,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154740,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if you were able to create it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156720,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you'd discover that that ... is actually unstable... that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160620,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "any sort of perturbation would push that empty vacuum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164900,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into something where the vacuum is actually\nfull of quantum field fluctuations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169840,
    "dDurationMs": 3220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, this may not be as strange as it first appears..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173060,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, consider a permanent magnet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175420,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It has a magnetic field around it\nat low energy, at room temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180200,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not  because the individual little magnetic moments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183020,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of all the atoms inside are lined up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185240,
    "dDurationMs": 1540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you were to heat it up,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186780,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you would give thermal energy to all those particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189480,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And at a certain point, called the Curie Temperature,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192100,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they would be so randomly aligned"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194360,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that there would no longer be an overall magnetic field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197960,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it actually takes energy to get rid\nof the permanent magnetic field."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202760,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hmm, this is just like the quantum vacuum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205600,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And undertanding how the quantum\nvacuum fluctuations work"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209360,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gives us a sense of what the fundamental particles do,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212900,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like 'where are you most likely to find a quark?'"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216240,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it turns out that the quark\nlikes to sit on top of those lumps."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220860,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now those lumps come into and out of existence\nfairly quickly and so ..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225300,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we like to think of the quarks as hopping\nfrom one lump over to the next lump, as it appears,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230040,
    "dDurationMs": 1260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then on to another one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231700,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I like to think of it as a hiker trying to\ncross a stream that's running around..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 238420,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every now and then a stone pops up\nbecause the water swirled around it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242380,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you put your foot there...\nYou're looking for the next spot..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245100,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you go quickly enough,\nyou might not get your feet wet..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247900,
    "dDurationMs": 5780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Uh, so I think quarks are very much do... well we know quarks are very much doing the same thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253680,
    "dDurationMs": 6360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So while it is true that you and I and all of the other atoms in the universe are mostly empty space,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260040,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it is also true that empty space isn't truly empty..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264260,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in fact it is these vacuum fluctuations\nwhich are essential for our existence."
    } ]
  } ]
}
